# Jaguar XJ Series 2 four-door saloon, 1973-1979.
#
# The 1973 revision of the XJ: a raised front bumper with the grille above it,
# a smaller grille, the front quarter light retained, horizontal grille bars and
# reversing lamps moved into the rear clusters. The long-wheelbase shell is
# modelled, matching the photographed car.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_XJ
#
# Dimensions 4.947 x 1.772 x 1.372 m, wheelbase 2.864 m (long-wheelbase
# saloon; the short-wheelbase car is 2.762 m to 1974).
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation exists in the pack. The side
# image is a front three-quarter about 45-50 degrees off the centre line, the
# most side-on Series 2 saloon found; the flank is reconciled against the front
# and rear three-quarters within the published dimensions. The photographed car
# carries non-original alloy wheels and a side stripe, which are not copied.
#
# Colours: grade (d), Jaguar BLVC paint-code tables rather than a UK brochure.
# British Racing Green 254, Regency Red TDD, Old English White NDB and
# Silver Sand 280 are period names. Weights 11, 10, 10, 9, total 40,
# provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 200 km/h. Comfort 120/510, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 120. Classes 3,4.
# Dates 1973-1979 production, road tail staggered 1994-1996.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-xj-series2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-xj-series2.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-xj-series2/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: no true side elevation exists; the side image is a front
# three-quarter about 45-50 degrees off. The flank was reconciled against both
# three-quarters and the published dimensions. The photographed car's
# non-original alloy wheels and side stripe are not copied. Lamp and grille detail
# is simplified at sprite scale. Reversing lamps sit inboard of the corner
# clusters, as the photographs show.


obj=citycar
name=JaguarXJSeries2(BritishRacingGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=11
intro_year=1973
intro_month=9
retire_year=1996
retire_month=6
speed=200
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=120
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=510

